_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":93.4,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.0035762778234463832,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":54.5,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.09585975382320029,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.02431,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":16.2,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":["paper"],"description_full":"Intuit Inc. provides financial management, payments and capital, compliance, and marketing products and services in the United States. The company operates in two segments: Global Business Solutions and Consumer. Its Global Business Solutions segment provides QuickBooks services, which include financial and business management online services, desktop software, payroll solutions, time tracking, merchant payment processing and bill pay solutions, checking accounts, and financing services for small and mid-market businesses; and Mailchimp, a marketing automation and customer relationship management. The Consumer segment provides TurboTax, a do-it-yourself and assisted income tax preparation products and services; Credit Karma, a personal finance solution that provides recommendations for credit card, home, auto, and personal loan, and insurance products; online savings and checking accounts; and access to its credit scores and reports, credit and identity monitoring, credit report dispute, credit building tools, debt pay-down assistance, credit card rewards optimization, and connected account capabilities. This segment also offers ProTax offerings which include Lacerte, ProSeries, and ProFile desktop tax-preparation software products; and ProConnect Tax Online, electronic tax filing service, and bank products and related services. It sells products and services through direct sales channels, multichannel shop-and-buy experiences, online application stores, and partner and other channels. Intuit Inc. has a strategic collaboration with Aprio, LLP to develop AI-powered solutions designed to help identify tax planning opportunities, benchmark business performance, improve financial visibility, and support more informed decision-making across industries, including construction, dental, wealth management, and tax. Intuit Inc. was founded in 1983 and is headquartered in Mountain View, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Sasan K. Goodarzi | CEO, President & Chairman | Age 57 | Compensation: $3.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 18K people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 12%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $466K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $111K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Intuit Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $91.3B market cap on $21.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years and +16% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 15% against a 10% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $8.7B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 40 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.94\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 23\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 7.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.4% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Significant goodwill (38% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 21% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 29% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 20% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","14 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Has Intuit (INTU) Fallen Far Enough To Sit Below Fair Value?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/software/nasdaq-intu/intuit/news/has-intuit-intu-fallen-far-enough-to-sit-below-fair-value","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794586488.19,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.607,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Intuit (INTU) Could Be 39% Undervalued On Earnings Focus","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/intuit-intu-could-39-undervalued-161043197.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794586243.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.361,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"UNIVEST FINANCIAL Corp Sells 3,736 Shares of Intuit Inc. $INTU","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/univest-financial-corp-sells-3736-shares-of-intuit-inc-intu.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794565981.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.878,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"If You Invested $1000 In Intuit Stock 20 Years Ago, You Would Have This Much Today","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/11/63227875/if-you-invested-1000-intuit-stock-20-years-ago-you-would-have-much-today","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794526215.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What solopreneurs need to know about tracking mileage","source":"cnbc.com","link":"https://www.cnbc.com/select/what-solopreneurs-need-to-know-about-tracking-mileage/","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794611808.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"The AI trade faces big tests next week, starting with Nvidia earnings and capped by Anthropic IPO","source":"cnbc.com","link":"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/13/stock-market-next-week-outlook-for-nov-16-20-2026.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794600259.0,"